Description: minimal Qt6 font viewer with a console-rendering preview
 qfontviewer is a small Qt6 Widgets application for browsing installed fonts.
 It links only qt6-base (no GNOME/KDE libraries, no QML, no Python).
 .
 Its console-approximation mode renders a font at a chosen pixel size with
 antialiasing and hinting disabled, magnified nearest-neighbor, with overlay
 lines and an objective clipping readout - so you can tell whether glyphs such
 as the underscore get clipped at small sizes before committing a font to a
 terminal or virtual console. It also offers a glyph grid and side-by-side
 comparison of two families.
